        "id": 1561214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T22:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding a new ApplicationExitInfo record, since the \"output\" should have included the records with native crashes, maybe we could just check if there is a record in the \u0027output\u0027 with REASON_CRASH_NATIVE, and its UID/PID matches with one of the records in the mTombstones, if yes, call `setNativeTombstonePfd` on that one",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a71cec61_4cca5832",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/os/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T23:54:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are 2 problems with this:\n\n1. the lifetimes of REASON_CRASH_NATIVE and the proto tombstone aren\u0027t the same: there\u0027s a window at the beginning of the crash where we\u0027ll have a REASON_CRASH_NATIVE, but no proto tombstone yet. If an app that forks a child and waits for it to return and then notices that it crashed, getHistoricalProcessExitReasons might give them a REASON_CRASH_NATIVE report without a proto tombstone, which will then gain one if it calls later. If other things crash, the proto tombstones can get deleted by other things crashing, which means the same REASON_CRASH_NATIVE can go from not having a proto tombstone to having one, back to not having one.\n\n2. there\u0027s a potential mismatch there: if the PID gets reused, we might attach the proto tombstone to the wrong crash (but that should be extremely rare). \n\nI think the most common use of apps using the proto tombstones is going to be an app searching only for proto tombstones to upload to their crash reporting, so it\u0027s probably better for us to separate them out more clearly?",
      "parentUuid": "a40b974e_0b1a36a3",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8adb097_a7ccbb3d",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/os/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 263,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T00:44:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the app forks a child process, the system_server wouldn\u0027t be aware of that because all the managed processes are supposed to be forked via zygote (or app zygote). I\u0027m not sure if we should support this case here, but for previous release, crash reports from the child processes are not supported via the public API, so I\u0027d prefer to ignore the child process thing because a) it\u0027s a grey area that it does work but we don\u0027t formally support it b) parent process should be able to debug the child process IIRC.\n\nFor the case that the proto tombstone could be gone because it\u0027s deleted by other crashes, just for confirmation, as here we\u0027re holding a r/w fd to that file, it should remain there even if it\u0027s \"unlinked\" by the tombstoned ? And if it\u0027s really gone, I think the race condition here also applies to the REASON_CRASH_NATIVE_STRUCTURED ?\n\nFor the PID reuse, I guess we can compare the timestamp to further narrow it down?\n\nCurrently the typically use case is that, app crashes and restarts, and at the beginning of the start, it\u0027ll call the API to see what caused the last crash, it\u0027ll extract whatever information the API returns and do its own crash reporting. Having two distinct records (REASON_CRASH_NATIVE_STRUCTURED and REASON_CRASH_NATIVE) for a single crash would be a little bit confusing IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "a71cec61_4cca5832",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dc864b6_cbc42abe",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/os/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
