      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T22:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a question, if an app is holding a readonly FD to this proto file (it gets via our new API ), will this function call cause any negative impact ?",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ed636b7_5bbdba95",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/os/NativeTombstoneManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 329,
      "author": {
        "id": 1079148
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T23:54:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The file will become 0-length, so if they\u0027re reading the file, it\u0027ll get truncated. There\u0027s a potential crash if they have the file mmapped and they read from memory.\n\nHowever, this only gets called via the app getting uninstalled or `am clear-exit-info`, so it shouldn\u0027t actually happen?",
      "parentUuid": "8dc864b6_cbc42abe",
      "revId": "8c3c7a9ba5537aba40b6413757e9a96f93c17a34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
